{"authored" [{"question" "q-37870" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $\\,T\\,$ is a linear transformation and $\\,T([\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 16\\end{aligned}])=[\\begin{aligned}28 \\\\ -20\\end{aligned}]$, then find $\\,T([\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948957/state.json" "file_sha256" "2e413607df37daceb6792959024f6c91ad3c91de05fe6ce68bf34c31ed306d2e" "basis" 559 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948957/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-37870" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since $\\,T\\,$ is a linear transformation, it must satisfy $\\,T(kv)=kT(v).$ Noting that $[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 16\\end{aligned}]=4[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}],$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T([\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 16\\end{aligned}]) & =T(4[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}])=4T([\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since we're told that \n\n$$\nT([\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 16\\end{aligned}])=[\\begin{aligned}28 \\\\ -20\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nwe must have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4T([\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]) & =[\\begin{aligned}28 \\\\ -20\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T([\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]) & =\\frac{1}{4}[\\begin{aligned}28 \\\\ -20\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T([\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]) & =[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948957/state.json" "file_sha256" "2e413607df37daceb6792959024f6c91ad3c91de05fe6ce68bf34c31ed306d2e" "basis" 559 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948957/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-37870" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :