\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,T({v}_{2})=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]$, then find $T({v}_{1}).$\n\n| $T({v}_{1})=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} |  |  |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948957/state.json" "file_sha256" "2e413607df37daceb6792959024f6c91ad3c91de05fe6ce68bf34c31ed306d2e" "basis" 559 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948957/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-317722" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since $T$ is a linear transformation, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(-kv+hw)=T(-kv)+T(hw)=-kT(v)+hT(w)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor any vectors $v$ and $w.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(-6{v}_{1}+5{v}_{2}) & =-6T({v}_{1})+5T({v}_{2}) \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ -39\\end{aligned}] & =-6T({v}_{1})+5[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\ 6T({v}_{1}) & =5[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ -39\\end{aligned}] \\\\ 6T({v}_{1}) & =[\\begin{aligned}20 \\\\ -15\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ -39\\end{aligned}] \\\\ 6T({v}_{1}) & =[\\begin{aligned}12 \\\\ 24\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T({v}_{1}) & =\\frac{1}{6}[\\begin{aligned}12 \\\\ 24\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T({v}_{1}) & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948957/state.json" "file_sha256" "2e413607df37daceb6792959024f6c91ad3c91de05fe6ce68bf34c31ed306d2e" "basis" 559 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948957/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-317722" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948957/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "da2ce15eaa626f2f693e7a66198c89e98a1b8f05a0562c5355846066169e6d49" "basis" 559 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948957/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-317722" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948957/state.json" "file_sha256" "2e413607df37daceb6792959024f6c91ad3c91de05fe6ce68bf34c31ed306d2e" "basis" 559 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948957/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-317722" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948957/state.json" "file_sha256" "2e413607df37daceb6792959024f6c91ad3c91de05fe6ce68bf34c31ed306d2e" "basis" 559 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948957/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-317817" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider a linear transformation $\\,T\\,.$ If $\\,T(3{v}_{1}+{v}_{2})=[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 13\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,T({v}_{2})=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}]$, then find $T({v}_{1}).$\n\n| $T({v}_{1})=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} |  |  |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948957/state.json" "file_sha256" "2e413607df37daceb6792959024f6c91ad3c91de05fe6ce68bf34c31ed306d2e" "basis" 559 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948957/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-317817" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since $T$ is a linear transformation, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(kv+w)=T(kv)+T(w)=kT(v)+T(w)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor any vectors $v$ and $w.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(3{v}_{1}+{v}_{2}) & =3T({v}_{1})+T({v}_{2}) \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 13\\end{aligned}] & =3T({v}_{1})+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}] \\\\ 3T({v}_{1}) & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 13\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}] \\\\ 3T({v}_{1}) & =[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T({v}_{1}) & =\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T({v}_{1}) & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948957/state.json" "file_sha256" "2e413607df37daceb6792959024f6c91ad3c91de05fe6ce68bf34c31ed306d2e" "basis" 559 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948957/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-317817" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948957/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "da2ce15eaa626f2f693e7a66198c89e98a1b8f05a0562c5355846066169e6d49" "basis" 559 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948957/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-317817" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948957/state.json" "file_sha256" "2e413607df37daceb6792959024f6c91ad3c91de05fe6ce68bf34c31ed306d2e" "basis" 559 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948957/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-317817" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948957/state.json" "file_sha256" "2e413607df37daceb6792959024f6c91ad3c91de05fe6ce68bf34c31ed306d2e" "basis" 559 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948957/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-317817" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948957/state.json" "file_sha256" "2e413607df37daceb6792959024f6c91ad3c91de05fe6ce68bf34c31ed306d2e" "basis" 559 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948957/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-317817" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948957/state.json" "file_sha256" "2e413607df37daceb6792959024f6c91ad3c91de05fe6ce68bf34c31ed306d2e" "basis" 559 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948957/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-317833" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider a linear transformation $\\,T\\,.$ If $\\,{v}_{1}+{v}_{2}=0\\,$ and $\\,T({v}_{1})=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\\,$, find $\\,T(6{v}_{1}-7{v}_{2}).$\n\n| $\\,T(6{v}_{1}-7{v}_{2})=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} |  |  |\n|  | {{field-3}} |  |  |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948957/state.json" "file_sha256" "2e413607df37daceb6792959024f6c91ad3c91de05fe6ce68bf34c31ed306d2e" "basis" 559 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948957/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-317833" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, since ${v}_{1}+{v}_{2}=0,$ we have that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6{v}_{1}-7{v}_{2} & =13{v}_{1}-7{v}_{1}-7{v}_{2} \\\\  & =13{v}_{1}-7({v}_{1}+{v}_{2}) \\\\  & =13{v}_{1}-7(0) \\\\  & =13{v}_{1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nT(6{v}_{1}-7{v}_{2})=T(13{v}_{1}).\n$$\n\nNow, since $T$ is a linear transformation, we have that $T(kv)=kT(v).$ So \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(13{v}_{1}) & =13T({v}_{1}) \\\\  & =13[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}52 \\\\ -13 \\\\ 39\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn conclusion, $T(6{v}_{1}-7{v}_{2})=[\\begin{aligned}52 \\\\ -13 \\\\ 39\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948957/state.json" "file_sha256" "2e413607df37daceb6792959024f6c91ad3c91de05fe6ce68bf34c31ed306d2e" "basis" 559 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948957/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-317833" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948957/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "da2ce15eaa626f2f693e7a66198c89e98a1b8f05a0562c5355846066169e6d49" "basis" 559 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948957/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-317833" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948957/state.json" "file_sha256" "2e413607df37daceb6792959024f6c91ad3c91de05fe6ce68bf34c31ed306d2e" "basis" 559 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/refere