  & =[\\begin{aligned}({x}_{1}+{y}_{1})+({x}_{2}+{y}_{2}) \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{y}_{1} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2}+{y}_{2} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =T[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{1}\\end{aligned}]+T[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}].\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{T}$ is a linear transformation.\n\nAs a result, all three statements are true." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948957/state.json" "file_sha256" "2e413607df37daceb6792959024f6c91ad3c91de05fe6ce68bf34c31ed306d2e" "basis" 559 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948957/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-170638" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948957/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "da2ce15eaa626f2f693e7a66198c89e98a1b8f05a0562c5355846066169e6d49" "basis" 559 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948957/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-170638" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948957/state.json" "file_sha256" "2e413607df37daceb6792959024f6c91ad3c91de05fe6ce68bf34c31ed306d2e" "basis" 559 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948957/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-170638" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "I and II only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948957/state.json" "file_sha256" "2e413607df37daceb679