}} |  |  |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039534/state.json" "file_sha256" "acc0de8d030b386af044b586d1aafbd40539fa3a3057430467a9f381371e0306"} {"question" "q-317716" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since $T$ is a linear transformation, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(-kv+hw)=T(-kv)+T(hw)=-kT(v)+hT(w)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor any vectors $v$ and $w.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(-5{v}_{1}+4{v}_{2}) & =-5T({v}_{1})+4T({v}_{2}) \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}23 \\\\ -24\\end{aligned}] & =-5T({v}_{1})+4[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\ 5T({v}_{1}) & =4[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}23 \\\\ -24\\end{aligned}] \\\\ 5T({v}_{1}) & =[\\begin{aligned}-12 \\\\ 16\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}23 \\\\ -24\\end{aligned}] \\\\ 5T({v}_{1}) & =[\\begin{aligned}-35 \\\\ 40\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T({v}_{1}) & =\\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}-35 \\\\ 40\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T({v}_{1}) & =[\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039534/state.json" "file_sha256" "acc0de8d030b386af044b586d1aafbd40539fa3a3057430467a9f381371e0306"} {"question" "q-317716" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039534/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ac4f50b8f701b6dffb9c4cd99045845bedf2eb03b2e18e969709210cedffd701"} {"question" "q-317716" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039534/state.json" "file_sha256" "acc0de8d030b386af044b586d1aafbd40539fa3a3057430467a9f381371e0306"} {"question" "q-317716" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-7"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039534/state.json" "file_sha256" "acc0de8d030b386af044b586d1aafbd40539fa3a3057430467a9f381371e0306"} {"question" "q-317716" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039534/state.json" "file_sha256" "acc0de8d030b386af044b586d1aafbd40539fa3a3057430467a9f381371e0306"} {"question" "q-317716" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "8"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039534/state.json" "file_sha256" "acc0de8d030b386af044b586d1aafbd40539fa3a3057430467a9f381371e0306"} {"question" "q-74782" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider a linear transformation $\\,T\\,.$ If $\\,{v}_{1}+{v}_{2}=0\\,$ and $\\,T({v}_{2})=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}]\\,$, find $\\,T(11{v}_{1}+6{v}_{2}).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039534/state.json" "file_sha256" "acc0de8d030b386af044b586d1aafbd40539fa3a3057430467a9f381371e0306"} {"question" "q-74782" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we have that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}11{v}_{1}+6{v}_{2} & =11{v}_{1}+11{v}_{2}-5{v}_{2} \\\\  & =11({v}_{1}+{v}_{2})-5{v}_{2} \\\\  & =11(0)-5{v}_{2} \\\\  & =-5{v}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nT(11{v}_{1}+6{v}_{2})=T(-5{v}_{2}).\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, since $T$ is a linear transformation, we have that $T(kv)=kT(v).$ So \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(-5{v}_{2}) & =-5T({v}_{2}) \\\\  & =-5[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-35 \\\\ -40 \\\\ -45\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn conclusion, $T(11{v}_{1}+6{v}_{2})=[\\begin{aligned}-35 \\\\ -40 \\\\ -45\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039534/state.json" "file_sha256" "acc0de8d030b386af044b586d1aafbd40539fa3a3057430467a9f381371e0306"} {"question" "q-74782" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039534/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ac4f50b8f701b6dffb9c4cd99045845bedf2eb03b2e18e969709210cedffd701"} {"question" "q-74782" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039534/state.json" "file_sha256" "acc0de8d030b386af044b586d1aafbd40539fa3a3057430467a9f381371e0306"} {"question" "q-74782" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-35 \\\\ -40 \\\\ -45\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-42 \\\\ -48 \\\\ -54\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ -8 \\\\ -9\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}35 \\\\ 40 \\\\ 45\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}42 \\\\ 48 \\\\ 54\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039534/state.json" "file_sha256" "acc0de8d030b386af044b586d1aafbd40539fa3a3057430467a9f381371e0306"} {"question" "q-74782" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}-35 \\\\ -40 \\\\ -45\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039534/state.json" "file_sha256" "acc0de8d030b386af044b586d1aafbd40539fa3a3057430467a9f381371e0306"} {"question" "q-74777" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider a linear transformation $\\,T\\,.$ If $\\,{v}_{1}+{v}_{2}=0\\,$ and $\\,T({v}_{1})=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 13 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]\\,$, find $\\,T(41{v}_{1}+37{v}_{2}).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039534/state.json" "file_sha256" "acc0de8d030b386af044b586d1aafbd40539fa3a3057430467a9f381371e0306"} {"question" "q-74777" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, since ${v}_{1}+{v}_{2}=0,$ we have that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}41{v}_{1}+37{v}_{2} & =37{v}_{1}+4{v}_{1}+37{v}_{2} \\\\  & =37({v}_{1}+{v}_{2})+4{v}_{1} \\\\  & =37(0)+4{v}_{1} \\\\  & =4{v}_{1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nT(41{v}_{1}+37{v}_{2})=T(4{v}_{1}).\n$$\n\nNow, since $T$ is a linear transformation, we have that $T(kv)=kT(v).$ So \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(4{v}_{1}) & =4T({v}_{1}) \\\\  & =4[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 13 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-16 \\\\ 52 \\\\ -28\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn conclusion, $T(41{v}_{1}+37{v}_{2})=[\\begin{aligned}-16 \\\\ 52 \\\\ -28\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039534/state.json" "file_sha256" "acc0de8d030b386af044b586d1aafbd40539fa3a3057430467a9f381371e0306"} {"question" "q-74777" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039534/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ac4f50b8f701b6dffb9c4cd99045845bedf2eb03b2e18e969709210cedffd701"} {"question" "q-74777" "field" "selection" "attribute" "ans