ue" "First, since ${v}_{1}+{v}_{2}=0,$ we have that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6{v}_{1}-7{v}_{2} & =13{v}_{1}-7{v}_{1}-7{v}_{2} \\\\  & =13{v}_{1}-7({v}_{1}+{v}_{2}) \\\\  & =13{v}_{1}-7(0) \\\\  & =13{v}_{1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nT(6{v}_{1}-7{v}_{2})=T(13{v}_{1}).\n$$\n\nNow, since $T$ is a linear transformation, we have that $T(kv)=kT(v).$ So \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(13{v}_{1}) & =13T({v}_{1}) \\\\  & =13[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}52 \\\\ -13 \\\\ 39\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn conclusion, $T(6{v}_{1}-7{v}_{2})=[\\begin{aligned}52 \\\\ -13 \\\\ 39\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039534/state.json" "file_sha256" "acc0de8d030b386af044b586d1aafbd40539fa3a3057430467a9f381371e0306"} {"question" "q-317833" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039534/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ac4f50b8f701b6dffb9c4cd99045845bedf2eb03b2e18e969709210cedffd701"} {"question" "q-317833" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039534/state.json" "file_sha256" "acc0de8d030b386af044b586d1aafbd40539fa3a3057430467a9f381371e0306"} {"question" "q-317833" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "52"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039534/state.json" "file_sha256" "acc0de8d030b386af044b586d1aafbd40539fa3a3057430467a9f381371e0306"} {"question" "q-317833" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type